    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4dc55eee_672cb65b",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 1624,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-21T13:31:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still find this very ad-hoc, and really don\u0027t like that Tethering is using some boolean in its IpServer to track some state, and that the stop() path ends up containing a start() path.\n\nOne way that I would find better:\n - Add a state in IpServer such as WaitingForRestartState\n - Instead of adding methods in IpServer.Callback, send mPrivateAddressCoordinator to each IpServer in its constructor\n - Have each IpServer register (for conflict notifications) to mPrivateAddressCoordinator, so instead of having ArrayMap\u003cString, IpPrefix\u003e mDownstreamPrefixMap, you just have ArrayList\u003cIpServer\u003e or LinkedHashSet\u003cIpServer\u003e\n - Instead of returning a list of conflicting interfaces, PrivateAddressCoordinator#updateUpstreamPrefix directly sends .notifyPrefixConflicts() to the IpServer (and returns void)\n - When receiving notifyPrefixConflicts(), the IpServer transitions to WaitingForRestartState and calls stopTetheringInternal() on Tethering in State#enter()\n - Once IpServer receives CMD_INTERFACE_DOWN  in WaitingForRestartState, it calls enableTetheringInternal() (so you\u0027d have new internal start/stop methods on IpServer.Callbacks) \n\n\nThis way state is tracked as usual (with a StateMachine state), and IpServer just has normal start / stop mechanics.\nIt also gives a clear role to PrivateAddressCoordinator: IpServers register to it to receive conflict notifications, and Tethering just notifies it of new upstream prefixes; so all the conflict detection logic is in PrivateAddressCoordinator.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1621,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1624,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "7127cb0a8650ca492988ae24b7d09117e1f6152a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
